Carafe: SuspendThread works as on Windows. The server sets the request first, then holds a thread that is inside
the kernel, giving the registers of its call at once, or pauses one that runs program code; a thread paused on its
way back from a call gives the registers it returns with. GetThreadContext waits for the thread's state word to
change rather than polling, a thread that only waits in the server is held the same way, and the snapshot of a
thread's runtime registers is gone. The exception handler marks the thread as no longer on its way back from a
call. A thread being terminated is alerted, so an alert wait ends at once and the thread ends on its way out.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

